---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Why Talon',href:'/why-talon/'}];
const reasons=[
  ['Group-first from the beginning','We plan around the organizer, the traveler mix, the likely headcount, and the reason these people are traveling together.'],
  ['Support beyond booking','Reservations are only part of the work. We also focus on participant information, readiness, supplier coordination, and the operational handoffs that make group travel easier to run.'],
  ['Active without the performance theater','A trip can be demanding, comfortable, beginner-friendly, cultural, skill-based, or a mixture. We describe the actual activity rather than forcing everything into an “extreme adventure” identity.'],
  ['Local specialists where they matter','Technical instruction, mountain guiding, diving, destination operations, and other specialist services are coordinated with appropriate local providers rather than pretending one company does every job everywhere.'],
  ['Clearer organizer workload','We design the planning process so the group leader has fewer disconnected suppliers, fewer repeated explanations, and a more coherent path from interest to departure.'],
  ['Preparation is part of the trip','Documents, equipment, fitness, activity prerequisites, rooming, arrivals, and final information are treated as operational work, especially for active and specialist journeys.'],
  ['Worldwide scope, specific trip design','We can plan globally without pretending every destination is interchangeable. Route, season, support, supplier model, and local realities drive each itinerary.'],
  ['One relationship that can expand','A group can start with a single private trip and later develop recurring departures, learn-to programs, annual club journeys, or new travel formats without rebuilding the relationship from scratch.']
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Why Plan Group Travel With Talon Expeditions" description="Why clubs, communities, teams, and private groups use Talon Expeditions for group-first travel planning, active and experience-led trip design, organizer support, and traveler preparation." image={images.wildlife} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.wildlife}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Why Talon Expeditions</p><h1 class="section-title">A group travel partner should make the trip clearer before it makes it bigger.</h1><p>Our value is not a slogan about unforgettable travel. It is a planning model built around the organizer, the travelers, and the practical work required to turn a good idea into a viable journey.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell definition-grid"><div class="definition-sticky"><p class="eyebrow">The difference</p><h2>We are built around supported group travel, not volume tour inventory.</h2></div><div class="definition-body"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>Why choose Talon Expeditions for a private group trip?</h2><p>Talon Expeditions combines custom trip design with organizer support, traveler preparation, and destination-specific supplier coordination. The model is particularly useful for clubs, communities, teams, and groups planning active, skill-based, cultural, or hosted journeys that involve more complexity than a simple hotel-and-flight booking.</p></div><p>Large group-tour brands are useful when travelers want to select from an established calendar of fixed departures. Independent planning is useful when a small group wants full control and is comfortable managing the details itself. Talon sits in a different space: groups that want the trip shaped around them and want meaningful support without losing the character of the experience.</p><p>That means being explicit about what the trip requires, where specialist partners are involved, how group size changes the plan, what travelers need to prepare, and how the organizer’s workload is handled.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">What drives the model</p><h2 class="section-title">Eight practical reasons groups work with us.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">These are operating principles, not claims that depend on fabricated awards, ratings, or traveler counts.</p></div><div class="donor-grid">{reasons.map((item,index)=><div class="donor-card"><span class="card-index">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{item[0]}</h3><p>{item[1]}</p></div>)}</div></div></section>
  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="shell mission-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Industry infrastructure</p><h2 class="section-title">Travel should feel personal to the group and professional behind the scenes.</h2><p style="color:#aaa">Talon Expeditions operates within the wider Talon Group and maintains travel-industry credentials and relationships that support trip planning and booking capabilities. Specific suppliers and operator relationships vary by itinerary.</p></div><div class="credentials"><div class="credential" style="background:#181311;color:#fff"><strong>CLIA</strong><span style="color:#aaa">Cruise-industry access and relationships</span></div><div class="credential" style="background:#181311;color:#fff"><strong>IATA</strong><span style="color:#aaa">Air-travel industry infrastructure</span></div><div class="credential" style="background:#181311;color:#fff"><strong>ARC</strong><span style="color:#aaa">U.S. travel-industry infrastructure</span></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell split-copy-image"><div class="split-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.group}')`}></div><div><p class="eyebrow">A different kind of proof</p><h2 class="section-title">A planning method you can evaluate before you book.</h2><p class="section-copy">A travel relationship should be understandable before a traveler is asked to trust it. We explain the planning method, the role of local specialists, the traveler-preparation process, and the boundaries of the service so organizers can evaluate how the relationship will work in practice.</p><p class="section-copy">Our public proof layer centers on operational clarity: what we plan, who we serve, how the process works, where local specialists fit, and what travelers should expect before they commit. Attributable trip stories and traveler feedback are published when they can be shown with useful context.</p><a class="button" href="/how-it-works/">See How Planning Works</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="feature-band" style={`background-image:url('${images.coast}')`}><div class="shell"><div class="band-copy"><p class="eyebrow">The trip should still feel like yours</p><h2 class="section-title">Support should remove friction without removing personality.</h2><p>Private group travel is valuable because the people already have a reason to be together. Our job is to support that reason with a better travel structure, not turn every community into the same tour group.</p></div></div></section>
  <PlanningCTA title="If you want the trip shaped around the group, start there." />
</BaseLayout>
